Date: Tue, 9 Nov 2077 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Do not log unsafe terrain read during worldgen

Adds log-to-console.unsafe-terrain-read (default: false), letting the
"Detected unsafe terrain read during worldgen" warning be suppressed.

This warning is commonly triggered by third-party structure/feature
datapacks (e.g. Terralith's fortified_village) that read terrain
outside the write radius guaranteed for the current generation step.
It does not indicate a Leaf/Paper bug and is not actionable from the
server side, so by default it is now silenced. It can be re-enabled
per world/globally to help diagnose datapack terrain-read issues.

Also throttles the warning to once per WorldGenRegion instance instead
of once per offending read, matching the existing "setBlock in a far
chunk" warning's throttling behavior, in case it is re-enabled.

